## Interlude / Side B — English Translation: Chapters 21–25

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 21 — Secret Behind the Spool
################################################################################

translate en b21_001:
    "The wealthy man was gone. His heavy cologne slowly lost out to the scent of jasmine tea. On the teak counter, the cassette with the snapped tape lay where it fell — brown, tangled, silent."

translate en b21_002:
    "Kai was still staring at the tangled ribbon. Pak Ageng had already settled back into his rocking chair, calm as if that little storm had never blown through."

translate en b21_003:
    kai "Pak."

translate en b21_004:
    ageng "Hmm?"

translate en b21_005:
    kai "…Why does this shop exist?"

translate en b21_006a:
    ageng "{i}(picks up his teacup, takes a sip, and looks over the row of glass cabinets){/i} Good question, Kai. What do you think? Why would a shop like this sit at the end of a dead-end alley almost nobody walks down?"

translate en b21_007a:
    kai "I used to think this place was a lifesaver. {i}(traces the rim of his teacup){/i} For someone like me — scared to death of tomorrow — your tapes felt like something to hold onto. Like a promise everything would be okay. But… after seeing that guy just now, and after hanging out with Yara lately… I'm starting to wonder."

translate en b21_008a:
    ageng "{i}(smiles faintly; his rocking chair gives a soft creak){/i} People are fragile, Kai. Mostly because they can't see what's ahead. Uncertainty is an anxious mind's worst enemy. {i}(pause){/i} This shop isn't here to turn people into gods. It's here to be a mirror."

translate en b21_009a:
    kai "A mirror?"

translate en b21_010a:
    ageng "Yeah. A mirror to show you just how far anxiety can run your life. {i}(nods toward the broken tape on the counter){/i} That man just now — he figured if he could own tomorrow, he could hold the whole world in his fist. He wasn't looking for peace, Kai. He was looking for control. Total control. And life just wasn't built to be controlled like that."

translate en b21_011a:
    "Pak Ageng let out a long breath. His gaze softened as he looked at Kai."

translate en b21_012a:
    ageng "Think about it. What would it feel like if you knew, word for word, everything Yara was going to say tomorrow afternoon? If you knew the exact day, the exact minute, and the exact joke that's going to make you two laugh next week?"

translate en b21_013a:
    "Kai went quiet. He pictured it: Yara laughing at his joke — and him already knowing it was coming."

translate en b21_014a:
    kai "…Flat. {i}(quietly){/i} There'd be no surprise left."

translate en b21_015a:
    ageng "Exactly. {i}(nods firmly){/i} Knowing the future usually just spoils the surprise. What makes life good isn't some finish line already written down. It's the flutter in your chest as you walk ahead without knowing what's around the next corner."

translate en b21_016a:
    kai "{i}(looks up, eyes clearer now){/i} So… you let us misread the sounds on those tapes on purpose?"

translate en b21_017a:
    ageng "{i}(chuckles){/i} I just spin the tape, kid. It's your own heart that chooses whether to hear fear or hope. And today… I'm glad to see you finally stopped listening to tomorrow, and started listening to right now."

translate en b21_018a:
    "The rocking chair creaked softly. Outside, the dead-end alley was wet as ever. Yet for the first time, Kai sat inside that shop without feeling chased by tomorrow."

translate en b21_006b:
    ageng "{i}(sips his tea, gazing at the glass cabinets){/i} What do you think? Why would a shop like this sit down a dead-end alley nobody ever walks through?"

translate en b21_007b:
    kai "I used to think it was a lifesaver, Pak. For an anxious guy like me, those tapes felt like something to hold onto. Lately though… I'm starting to doubt it myself."

translate en b21_008b:
    ageng "{i}(smiles faintly){/i} People are fragile because they can't see ahead, Kai. This shop isn't here to turn people into gods. It's here to be a mirror."

translate en b21_009b:
    kai "A mirror?"

translate en b21_010b:
    ageng "A mirror to show you how far anxiety can run your life. That man just now wasn't looking for peace. He was looking for control. And life—"

translate en b21_011b:
    kai "{i}(checks his phone screen, sighing){/i} …It's Mom, Pak. Telling me to come home right now. Says it's almost dusk."

translate en b21_012b:
    ageng "Wes, head on home. Your mom's waiting."

translate en b21_013b:
    kai "Right when we were getting to the important part… You'll finish telling me tomorrow, right?"

translate en b21_014b:
    ageng "Tomorrow's tomorrow's business. {i}(smiles){/i} Go on home. Watch your step, the alley's slick."

translate en b21_015b:
    "Kai walked home with his head full of questions. That word \"mirror\" kept echoing in his mind — though a mirror for what, exactly, he hadn't gotten to hear the end of."

translate en b21_006c:
    ageng "Hmm?"

translate en b21_007c:
    kai "Nothing. Never mind, Pak. {i}(shakes his head quickly){/i} I… I just want to buy a regular cassette. For tomorrow."

translate en b21_008c:
    ageng "{i}(pauses for a moment, then smiles){/i} Alright."

translate en b21_009c:
    "Pak Ageng got up, pulled a single Regular Cassette from the shelf, and handed it over without another word. No story. No explanation."

translate en b21_010c:
    kai_hati "Why'd he smile like that… Like he already knew I'd run away from my own question."

translate en b21_011c:
    "The shop felt colder than usual that afternoon. Or maybe it was just Kai. He left earlier than normal — and for the first time, he wasn't rushing home to listen to tomorrow; he was running away from today."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 22 — Falling Water, Lingering Seconds
################################################################################

translate en b22_001:
    "The rain hit that afternoon without any warning. A sky that had just been overcast suddenly broke open — pouring so thick the end of the alley vanished behind white mist."

translate en b22_002:
    "Kai and Yara sprinted through the alley, skidding to a breathless stop under the wooden awning outside Toko Gema Masa. Behind them, the shop door was shut tight."

translate en b22_003:
    yara "{i}(catching her breath, setting her canvas gear bag down in the driest corner){/i} Totally soaked… {i}(checks inside her bag){/i} Good thing the recorder stayed dry."

translate en b22_004:
    "Yara's gray jacket had turned dark from the rain. A few damp strands of hair clung to her forehead and cheek. Kai leaned back against the cold brick wall, shrugging off his half-soaked jacket. The chill crept in, making him shiver a little."

translate en b22_005:
    "Then he glanced over — Yara sitting with her knees pulled to her chest on the narrow porch floor — and somehow the cold just disappeared."

translate en b22_006:
    kai_hati "The door's closed. We could easily knock. …Funny how neither of us actually wants to."

translate en b22_007:
    "Neither of them knocked. Neither called out for Pak Ageng. This tiny two-square-meter porch — they silently agreed — was enough. It was the whole world they needed that afternoon."

translate en b22_008:
    "Yara reached into her jacket pocket and pulled out her small pocket recorder. No boom mic this time — just that little device, balanced on her bent knees."

translate en b22_009:
    yara "Feels like a waste not to record rain like this. {i}(scans the porch){/i} Where do you think we'll catch the best sound?"

translate en b22_010a:
    yara "The gutter? {i}(nods, scooting her recorder closer to the dripping roof gutter){/i} True. The drops fall one by one, sounds like… a beat. Neat."

translate en b22_010b:
    yara "The leaves? {i}(laughs softly){/i} I'm starting to rub off on you, rek. {i}(sets the recorder beside the plant pot){/i} Listen — every single drop sounds different because the leaves keep swaying."

translate en b22_010c:
    yara "The umbrella? {i}(pulls a folding umbrella from her bag, opening it halfway on the porch floor){/i} Hmm… umbrella fabric is basically a drumhead. Take a listen."

translate en b22_011:
    yara "{i}(closes her eyes for a second){/i} There. That's the one."

translate en b22_012:
    yara "{i}(holds out one side of her big headphones without looking over){/i} Wanna listen?"

translate en b22_013:
    "Kai smiled faintly. He shifted closer until their chilled arms brushed together, and pressed the earcup to his left ear."

translate en b22_014:
    "Through Yara's recorder, the wild downpour turned intimate. Water dripping off the edge of the awning, landing in puddles with clear little notes. Yara's steady breathing right beside him. The soft rustle of fabric whenever either of them shifted slightly."

translate en b22_015:
    "Neither of them spoke. Under the spray of rain cooling Malang down, words felt unnecessary."

translate en b22_016:
    "Yara kept her eyes shut, soaking in the sound. Kai kept his open — watching the side of Yara's face in the dim yellow glow of the porch light."

translate en b22_017:
    kai_hati "Weird. I have no idea what tomorrow's going to look like. No idea about six months from now either. {i}(pause){/i} Still, right here, this one minute… I'm not scared. Not scared at all."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 23 — Echoes for the Past
################################################################################

translate en b23_001:
    "The downpour slowly eased up, leaving only a lazy patter of drops on the alley asphalt."

translate en b23_002:
    "Yara opened her eyes and slipped the headphones back around her neck. She looked down at the small recorder on her knees, then up at Kai."

translate en b23_003:
    yara "Kai."

translate en b23_004:
    kai "Yeah?"

translate en b23_005:
    yara "Let's make our own recording."

translate en b23_006:
    kai "Our own recording? For your portfolio again?"

translate en b23_007:
    yara "{i}(shakes her head, damp hair swaying){/i} Not for the portfolio. And not a forecast like Pak Ageng's tapes you used to buy."

translate en b23_007_p2:
    yara "{i}(reaches into her canvas bag, pulls out the blank red-cased cassette — the Type IV Metal from Pak Ageng — and snaps it into her portable recorder; click){/i} Let's record our voices right now. Not for the future, though. For the past."

translate en b23_008:
    kai "The past?"

translate en b23_009:
    yara "We send a message to our old selves. Proof… that we actually made it through. {i}(looks straight at Kai){/i} What do you say?"

translate en b23_010a:
    "Yara held out the small microphone right between their faces and pressed record. A tiny red indicator light blinked on — inside, the tape began to roll."

translate en b23_011a:
    yara "{i}(leans her lips close to the mic){/i} To Yara a month ago, standing alone at the bus stop with her hands clamped over her ears because she hated how loud the world was… {i}(smiles out toward the wet street){/i} Don't be scared of all that noise around you."

translate en b23_011a_p2:
    yara "One day, it's going to introduce you to someone who'll gladly haul this heavy tripod bag all over town for you. Without complaining once."

translate en b23_012a:
    "Yara nudged Kai's arm with her elbow. Your turn."

translate en b23_013a:
    kai_hati "Okay. For old Kai. The one locked up in his bedroom. Writing all those ridiculous letters. {i}(takes a breath){/i} What do I even say…"

translate en b23_014a:
    kai "{i}(speaks calmly into the mic){/i} To the Kai who locked himself in his room writing ridiculous goodbye letters because he was way too scared of tomorrow… Put the pen down. You're not going to die this Friday."

translate en b23_014a_p2:
    kai "In fact, you're actually going to start living the moment that stack of books crashes down. Just live today. The surprise waiting ahead of you is way better than any forecast."

translate en b23_015a:
    "Yara pressed stop. A small mechanical click. Their voices were now sealed onto that dark metal-coated tape — a recording that promised nothing about tomorrow, yet kept the happiness of this exact second locked safe inside."

translate en b23_016a:
    yara "{i}(gives him the warmest, most genuine smile Kai has ever seen){/i} Done. …Right now, our past selves are probably listening to this. And breathing a sigh of relief."

translate en b23_017a:
    kai "{i}(nods, warmth spreading all the way to his fingertips){/i} Yeah. Definitely relieved."

translate en b23_010b:
    kai "I'll… just listen, Yar. You go ahead. I don't know what to say yet."

translate en b23_011b:
    yara "{i}(looks at him for a beat, then nods without pushing){/i} Alright. Just listening counts as joining in too."

translate en b23_012b:
    "Yara pressed record and spoke her message alone — to Yara at the bus stop, hands clamped tight over her ears. Her voice was soft, and on her last sentence she glanced over at Kai with a smile."

translate en b23_013b:
    yara "…One day, it's going to introduce you to someone who'll gladly haul this heavy tripod bag all over town for you. Without complaining once. {i}(hits stop){/i} There. {i}(looks at Kai){/i} Whenever you figure out what you want to say, there's still plenty of tape left. We'll record again."

translate en b23_014b:
    kai "…Thanks, Yar."

translate en b23_015b:
    "The cassette only held one voice that afternoon. Still, Yara tucked it away just as carefully — as if it held two."

translate en b23_010c:
    kai "{i}(shakes his head slowly){/i} No, Yar. The past… just leave it back there. I don't want to talk to him."

translate en b23_011c:
    yara "{i}(goes quiet for a moment; not offended, just looking at him){/i} …Alright. That's okay."

translate en b23_012c:
    "Kai stood up, walked to the edge of the porch, and stepped out toward the mouth of the alley. Light raindrops dotted his jacket. Behind him, faint and distant, he could hear Yara recording by herself — quiet, far off, broken every so often by a soft laugh."

translate en b23_013c:
    kai_hati "She's laughing. Talking to her old self… and actually laughing. {i}(pause){/i} Why can't I do that?"

translate en b23_014c:
    "Kai waited at the mouth of the alley until the recording finished — listening to laughter from the shop porch he hadn't joined in on, standing under the exact same drizzle."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 24 — Whispers That Tempt Again
################################################################################

translate en b24_001:
    "That night, Kai lay in bed staring up at the ceiling. His room was a lot neater these days. Sitting nicely on his desk was the red-cased cassette — their recording for the past."

translate en b24_002:
    "He should have felt calm. Instead, a brand-new tightness was creeping across his chest."

translate en b24_003:
    kai_hati "I get it now. That warmth whenever our arms brush. That… sinking feeling every time the final bell rings. The way my eyes keep scanning the hallway for her. {i}(long pause){/i} I'm in love. Actually in love with Yara."

translate en b24_004:
    kai_hati "The problem is — she already made it clear. All these recordings are for her portfolio. To get into a music arts program out of town. Maybe even abroad. Right after final exams. Six months from now."

translate en b24_005:
    kai_hati "Six months. A hundred and eighty days. {i}(swallows){/i} After that… does my world just go silent all over again?"

translate en b24_006:
    "And right on cue, the anxiety in Kai's head started whispering again — pointing straight at one place: the special glass cabinet at Toko Gema Masa."

translate en b24_007:
    kai_hati "The red cassette. Six months ahead. If I buy it… I'll hear it. Whether Yara's laugh is still there or not. If it is, I can breathe easy. If it isn't… {i}(pause){/i} …at least I can start bracing for the heartbreak now."

translate en b24_008:
    "That afternoon, with a hesitant pace he knew way too well, Kai found himself standing in front of the shop's wooden door again. His hand trembled on the handle."

translate en b24_009a:
    "Pak Ageng was brewing black coffee, its bitter steam filling the room. He didn't look surprised to see Kai — though a flicker of quiet concern crossed his eyes at seeing that familiar worry back on Kai's face."

translate en b24_010a:
    ageng "You're back again, Kai. {i}(sets down his clay kettle){/i} Carrying a different kind of weight today."

translate en b24_011a:
    "Kai didn't sit down. He walked over to the special glass cabinet and stared at the Type IV Metal cassette labeled six months ahead, gleaming under the warm yellow bulb."

translate en b24_012a:
    kai "Pak… I want to buy another cassette."

translate en b24_013a:
    ageng "{i}(lets out a long sigh; walks over to stand beside Kai without looking at the cabinet){/i} What for, kid? Thought you'd already learned how to listen to today."

translate en b24_014a:
    kai "Today's too good, Pak. {i}(his eyes glisten, fixed on the red cassette){/i} And because it's so good… I'm terrified of losing it. I just want to know one thing. Six months from now — is Yara still in my future, or not? That's all. I just need one thing to be sure of."

translate en b24_015a:
    "Pak Ageng stayed quiet for a long moment. Then, without answering, he walked to the very back shelf, pulled out an old tape with a blank cover, and popped it into the player on the counter."

translate en b24_016a:
    ageng "Listen first. Decide after."

translate en b24_017a:
    "Laughter. Just laughter. A young woman laughing at something whose reason was long gone from the tape — cutting off mid-laugh, because that was all the ribbon had left to hold."

translate en b24_018a:
    kai "…Who was that, Pak?"

translate en b24_019a:
    ageng "{i}(softly, eyes fixed on the spinning cassette){/i} Siti. My wife. {i}(pause){/i} I used to stand right where you're standing, kid. Only back then, my glass cabinet was a radio. I was a sound technician. Thought if I could just capture every sound, nothing could ever be taken from me."

translate en b24_020a:
    ageng "Turns out you can keep the voice. Not the person."

translate en b24_021a:
    "The laughter on the tape had run out. All that remained was static hiss — and for the first time, Kai listened to that hiss without feeling the urge to fill it with predictions."

translate en b24_022a:
    kai "{i}(wipes his eyes roughly){/i} …I'm not buying it, Pak. Not today."

translate en b24_023a:
    ageng "{i}(gives one slow nod){/i} Go on. Heard Bukit Banyak looks nice this evening. Someone's waiting for you up there, isn't there?"

translate en b24_009b:
    "Kai's hand was already resting on the doorknob. The tiny bell overhead swayed a little — not quite enough to ring."

translate en b24_010b:
    kai_hati "No. Not today. {i}(lets go of the doorknob){/i} If I really need to talk… I should talk to her directly. Not to a cassette."

translate en b24_011b:
    "Kai turned around and walked back down the wet alley alone. Behind him, the shop light stayed on — and nobody ever knew how close he'd come to stepping inside."

translate en b24_009c:
    kai_hati "No. What's the point of pouring my heart out? Pak Ageng would probably just give me that knowing smile anyway. {i}(lets go of the doorknob){/i} I'll deal with it myself. Alone. Just like always."

translate en b24_011c:
    "Kai turned around and walked back down the wet alley alone. Behind him, the shop light stayed on — and nobody ever knew how close he'd come to stepping inside."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 25 — Shadows at Dusk's Edge
################################################################################

translate en b25_001:
    "The air up at the top of Bukit Banyak had a sharp bite to it. For Kai, though, the real chill was spreading from somewhere else — right inside his own chest."

translate en b25_002:
    "Yara sat on the wild grass, damp with evening dew. She'd just finished recording the wind brushing over the pine tops below them. Her headphones rested loose around her neck."

translate en b25_003:
    yara "{i}(watches the city lights flickering on one by one in the distance){/i} Look at that, Kai."

translate en b25_004:
    "She pointed toward the horizon, where the last orange streaks of dusk melted into night."

translate en b25_005:
    yara "Oh right — listen to this first. {i}(pulls out her pocket recorder, playing it at low volume){/i} From yesterday, on the shop porch. The rain we recorded."

translate en b25_006:
    yara "{i}(smiles){/i} Sounds good, doesn't it? Even though it's just rain on somebody's shop porch."

translate en b25_007:
    kai "…Yeah. Really good."

translate en b25_008:
    yara "Six months from now, I might be looking at a totally different view. A bigger city, unfamiliar sounds. {i}(her eyes shine, catching the last glow of dusk){/i} I want to record subway trains roaring through tunnels."

translate en b25_008_p2:
    yara "Thousands of strangers' footsteps at a crosswalk. The racket of a harbor at night. My portfolio's almost done, Kai. Feels like… the future ahead looks so bright."

translate en b25_009:
    "Yara turned to him, practically glowing. Kai couldn't match that spark. To Yara, six months ahead was an open gate. To Kai, six months ahead was a cliff edge."

translate en b25_010:
    kai "You… really want to leave, huh?"

translate en b25_011:
    yara "{i}(her smile slips; a faint crease appears between her brows){/i} Kai, this is my dream. I want to learn more about sound. About turning the world's noise into something alive. {i}(her hand brushes over Kai's ice-cold fingers){/i} Isn't that a good thing?"

translate en b25_012:
    "Yara's hand was warm. Somehow that warmth only made Kai's chest ache worse. He squeezed her fingers back, tight — as if holding on could keep time from moving."

translate en b25_013:
    kai "Yeah. It is. It's amazing. {i}(his voice goes hoarse; his eyes drift to the blurring city lights){/i} I'm just… I'm scared my world will go silent again once you leave. Scared I won't be able to hear that \"music\" anymore without you right here."

translate en b25_014b:
    "Yara studied him for a long beat. And Kai — who'd stood at the shop door yesterday and chosen to talk to her instead — took a breath."

translate en b25_015b:
    kai "Yar. There's something I want to tell you—"

translate en b25_016b:
    yara "{i}(waits){/i} …Yeah?"

translate en b25_017b:
    "The words caught in his throat. In Kai's head, the sentence was: {i}I'm terrified of losing you.{/i} What actually came out of his mouth was—"

translate en b25_018b:
    kai "…The wind up here. Yesterday in the rain on the porch, didn't it kind of sound like this?"

translate en b25_019b:
    yara "{i}(blinks){/i} …Hmm? {i}(pause; gives a small smile without pressing){/i} Different. Wind on the hill's thinner. Like… a held breath."

translate en b25_020b:
    "Yara flipped open her notebook and jotted something down. Quick, short. Kai tried to peek — she'd already snapped it shut."

translate en b25_021b:
    kai_hati "What'd she write? {i}(pause){/i} Why couldn't I just get one simple sentence out."

translate en b25_022:
    yara "{i}(shifts closer until their shoulders press together, then leans her head against his){/i} This world is never going to go silent, Kai. Even after I'm gone, all those sounds will still be here. Just promise me one thing: don't ever close your ears again."

translate en b25_023:
    "Kai shut his eyes tight. He caught the faint scent of Yara's hair, damp from the evening mist. Far below them, all of Malang glowed."

translate en b25_024:
    kai_hati "So this is what falling in love feels like. The most beautiful anxiety… and the sharpest hurt I've ever recorded."

translate en b25_025c:
    yara_pesan "Kai, so sorry, I can't make it up to the hill today. Sudden family stuff came up. Tomorrow, okay? Are you already up there? Be careful heading home."

translate en b25_026c:
    "Kai read the message twice. Then he sat down alone on the dew-damp grass, right on the exact spot where the two of them always sat."

translate en b25_027c:
    kai_hati "The city lights are coming on one by one. Pretty. {i}(pause){/i} She'd definitely have something to say about the sound of the wind. Or about… who knows. She always has something to say about stuff I used to think was completely ordinary."

translate en b25_028c:
    kai_hati "Six months from now, I might be sitting right here like this. Alone. Only difference is, by then there won't be a text message left to read twice."

translate en b25_029c:
    "Kai closed his eyes. The pine breeze drifted past. He didn't record anything, didn't tell anyone — just sat there holding onto his own fear until every single light in the city below had come on."
